# Classification / Odd One Out — In-Depth Guide — Part 8 of 16

[info title="Part 8 of 16"]
Continuing from the previous part. back to Part 7 (`classification-detailed-part-7`) · continue to Part 9 (`classification-detailed-part-9`).
[/info]

## 100. General Knowledge Classification

Questions may depend on factual categories.

Example:

```text
Mercury
Venus
Earth
Moon
```

Mercury, Venus and Earth are planets.

Moon is a satellite.

Answer = **Moon**.

---

## 101. Science Classification

```text
Oxygen
Nitrogen
Hydrogen
Water
```

Oxygen, nitrogen and hydrogen are elements.

Water is a compound.

**Answer: Water**

---

## 102. Chemistry Classification

```text
Gold
Silver
Copper
Sodium chloride
```

Gold, silver and copper are elements/metals.

Sodium chloride is a compound.

---

## 103. Biology Classification

```text
Heart
Lungs
Kidney
Femur
```

Heart, lungs and kidney are organs.

Femur is a bone.

---

## 104. Human Body Classification

```text
Eye
Ear
Nose
Heart
```

Eye, ear and nose are sensory organs.

Heart is primarily a circulatory organ.

**Answer: Heart**

---

## 105. Computer Classification

```text
Keyboard
Mouse
Monitor
Windows
```

Keyboard, mouse and monitor are hardware devices.

Windows is software/operating system.

**Answer: Windows**

---

## 106. Programming Classification

```text
Python
Rust
C++
HTML
```

Python, Rust and C++ are general-purpose programming languages.

HTML is a markup language.

**Answer: HTML**

---

## 107. File-Type Classification

```text
PNG
JPG
SVG
MP3
```

PNG, JPG and SVG are image formats.

MP3 is audio.

**Answer: MP3**

---

## 108. Operating System Classification

```text
Linux
Windows
macOS
Chrome
```

Linux, Windows and macOS are operating systems.

Chrome is a web browser.

**Answer: Chrome**

---

## 109. Tool vs Product Classification

```text
Hammer
Saw
Drill
Table
```

Hammer, saw and drill are tools.

Table is furniture.

---

## 110. Function-Based Trap

```text
Phone
Camera
Television
Spoon
```

Phone, camera and television are electronic devices.

Spoon is not.

---

## 111. Material-Based Trap

```text
Chair
Table
Cupboard
Iron
```

Chair, table and cupboard are furniture.

Iron is a material/metal.

---

## 112. Classification by Use

```text
Pen
Pencil
Eraser
Knife
```

Pen, pencil and eraser are commonly associated with writing/stationery.

Knife is a cutting tool.

---

## 113. Classification by Location

```text
Fish
Whale
Dolphin
Camel
```

Fish, whale and dolphin are associated with aquatic environments.

Camel is terrestrial.

---

## 114. Classification by Diet

```text
Cow
Goat
Deer
Lion
```

Cow, goat and deer are herbivores.

Lion is carnivorous.

**Answer: Lion**

---

## 115. Classification by Biological Group

```text
Whale
Dolphin
Bat
Dog
```

Whale, dolphin and dog are mammals, and bat is also a mammal, so there is no outlier.

This is an important lesson:

> **Do not assume the first apparent category is correct.**

---

## 116. Classification by Taxonomic Level

```text
Rose
Mango
Neem
Tiger
```

Rose, mango and neem are plants.

Tiger is animal.

---

## 117. Classification by Reproduction

Advanced science questions can distinguish:

- oviparous
- viviparous
- asexual reproduction
- seed-producing plants

The correct rule must be based on the question's intended syllabus.

---
